 "is_vocab": false,
 "stimulus_html": "From past data, it’s known that the probability that an individual owns a dog is 0.42. Three random people are asked if they own a dog. (Round answers to 3 decimal places).",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 457862,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Find the probability that all three people own a dog.\n",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "0.074\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "The probability that all three people own a dog will be equivalent to the probability that the first person owns a dog and the second person owns a dog and the third person owns a dog. This implies that we want to find the probability <span data-math=\"P\\left( {A\\;\\mathrm{and}\\;B\\;\\mathrm{and}\\;C} \\right)\"></span> where the events that each person owns a dog are considered to be independent from one another.<br>Thus the probability can be calculated as:<br>\n<span data-math=\"P\\left( {A\\;\\mathrm{and}\\;B\\;\\mathrm{and}\\;C} \\right) = P\\left( A \\right)\\cdot P\\left( B \\right)\\cdot P\\left( C \\right) = 0.42\\cdot 0.42\\cdot 0.42 = 0.074\"></span>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 457863,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Find the probability that none of the three people own a dog.\n\n",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "To find the probability that none of the three people own a dog, first find the probability for the event that a person owns a dog, and use the probability formula for the complement of an event: <br><span data-math=\"P\\left( {A'} \\right) = 1 - P\\left( A \\right) = 1 - 0.42 = 0.58\"></span><br>Next, find the probability that none of the three people own a dog as follows:<br><span data-math=\"P\\left( {A'\\;\\mathrm{and}\\;B'\\;\\mathrm{and}\\;C'} \\right) = P\\left( {A'} \\right)\\cdot P\\left( {B'} \\right)\\cdot P\\left( {C'} \\right) = 0.58 \\cdot 0.58\\cdot 0.58 = 0.195\"></span>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "0.195\n"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 457864,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Find the probability that at least one of the people owns a dog.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "The phrase “at least one” implies the condition of one or more successes. From a sample space perspective, one or more successes is the complement of “no successes.” Using the complement rule, we can write the following probability formula.<br><span data-math=\"P\\left( {\\mathrm{at}\\;\\mathrm{least}\\;\\mathrm{one}\\;\\mathrm{person}\\;\\mathrm{owns}\\;\\mathrm{a}\\;\\mathrm{dog}} \\right) = 1 - P\\left( {\\mathrm{none}\\;\\mathrm{own}\\;\\mathrm{a}\\;\\mathrm{dog}} \\right) = 1 - 0.195 = 0.805\"></span>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "0.805 "
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
